Description: Functions for fitting longitudinal functional joint models when
    a functional predictor is observed repeatedly together with a scalar
    longitudinal response and a time-to-event outcome. The package uses
    weighted-grid longitudinal functional principal component analysis to
    separate persistent between-subject variation from visit-specific
    within-subject variation, and estimates the resulting shared-current-value
    joint model by adjusted profile h-likelihood. It provides tools for model
    fitting, control specification, prediction, fitted values, residuals,
    coefficient and covariance extraction, summaries, visualization, and
    simulation-based data generation.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
